.TH __CHTTPCLIENT_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
__chttpclient_destroy \- internal destroy function
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

void __chttpclient_destroy(chttpcli cli);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Waits for all in-flight requests to complete, then closes all pooled
connections (both idle and TLS), frees the idle-connection pool,
destroys the client's TLS context, frees synchronisation primitives,
and frees the client struct.

Do not call directly; use the chttpclient_destroy macro, which also
sets the handle to NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_destroy (3),
.BR ___chttpclient_destroy (3)
